    <item>
      <title>Python Environment Managers: pip &#43; venv vs poetry &#43; pyenv vs uv</title>
      <link>http://localhost:50759/blog/python-env-managers/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Nov 2025 17:15:00 -0500</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:50759/blog/python-env-managers/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;ve been writing Python for a while, you&amp;rsquo;ve probably felt the pain of dependency hell. Your project works on your machine, breaks on your colleague&amp;rsquo;s, and then explodes in production. The culprit? Inconsistent Python environments and dependency management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are several ways to handle this. Let me walk you through the main approaches, their trade-offs, and why I&amp;rsquo;ve landed on &lt;code&gt;uv&lt;/code&gt; as my go-to tool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Are These Tools?&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;what-are-these-tools&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#what-are-these-tools&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Before we compare, let&amp;rsquo;s clarify what we&amp;rsquo;re actually talking about. There are two separate concerns here:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment Managers&lt;/strong&gt; handle which Python version you&amp;rsquo;re using. They let you have Python 3.10 for one project and Python 3.12 for another without conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Package Managers/Dependency Resolvers&lt;/strong&gt; handle your project dependencies. They install packages, track versions, and ensure reproducibility across machines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most setups combine both. Here&amp;rsquo;s what we&amp;rsquo;re comparing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;pip + venv&lt;/strong&gt;: The standard library approach. Minimal, built-in, but manual.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;poetry + pyenv&lt;/strong&gt;: The &amp;ldquo;professional&amp;rdquo; setup. Opinionated, feature-rich, battle-tested.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;uv&lt;/strong&gt;: The new kid. Fast, simple, and refreshingly straightforward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Contenders&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;the-contenders&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#the-contenders&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;pip + venv&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;pip--venv&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#pip--venv&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it is&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;venv&lt;/code&gt; is Python&amp;rsquo;s built-in virtual environment tool. &lt;code&gt;pip&lt;/code&gt; is the standard package installer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pros&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zero external dependencies. It&amp;rsquo;s all in the standard library.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simple to understand. Create a venv, activate it, install packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lightweight. No extra tooling to learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works everywhere Python works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cons&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manual version management. You have to download Python versions yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No lock file by default. &lt;code&gt;requirements.txt&lt;/code&gt; doesn&amp;rsquo;t guarantee reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slow dependency resolution. pip doesn&amp;rsquo;t always find the best version combinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tedious workflow. Activate/deactivate venvs manually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code&#34;&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;
&lt;table style=&#34;border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;python3.10 -m venv venv
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;source venv/bin/activate  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pip install -r requirements.txt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button
    class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50&#34;
    title=&#34;Copy code&#34;
  &gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lock file&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;requirements.txt&lt;/code&gt; (manual, not guaranteed to be reproducible)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;poetry + pyenv&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;poetry--pyenv&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#poetry--pyenv&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it is&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;pyenv&lt;/code&gt; manages Python versions. &lt;code&gt;poetry&lt;/code&gt; handles dependencies and project packaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pros&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatic Python version management. &lt;code&gt;.python-version&lt;/code&gt; file keeps everyone on the same version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lock files are first-class. &lt;code&gt;poetry.lock&lt;/code&gt; guarantees reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependency resolution is smart. Poetry understands complex version constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great for publishing packages. Poetry handles versioning and publishing to PyPI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Isolated by default. Each project gets its own environment automatically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cons&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steep learning curve. Multiple tools, multiple concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slower than you&amp;rsquo;d expect. Dependency resolution can take time on large projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opinionated structure. Poetry expects a certain project layout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overkill for simple scripts. Adding complexity for small projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configuration friction. &lt;code&gt;pyproject.toml&lt;/code&gt; has a lot of options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code&#34;&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;
&lt;table style=&#34;border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;13
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;14
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;15
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# Install pyenv&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;brew install pyenv  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# or your OS equivalent&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# Install Python version&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pyenv install 3.12.0
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;pyenv local 3.12.0
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# Install poetry&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;curl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python3 -
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# Create project&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;poetry new my_project
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;cd my_project
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;poetry add requests
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;poetry install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button
    class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50&#34;
    title=&#34;Copy code&#34;
