&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why I Chose uv&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;why-i-chose-uv&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#why-i-chose-uv&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve used all three approaches in production. Here&amp;rsquo;s why uv is my default now:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Transparent&lt;/strong&gt;: I understand exactly what&amp;rsquo;s happening. No magic, no hidden complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Fast&lt;/strong&gt;: Dependency resolution is so fast it&amp;rsquo;s almost instant. This matters when you&amp;rsquo;re iterating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Simple&lt;/strong&gt;: One tool, one mental model. No context switching between pyenv and poetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Good defaults&lt;/strong&gt;: Works well for new projects without configuration overhead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Compatible&lt;/strong&gt;: Uses standard &lt;code&gt;pyproject.toml&lt;/code&gt;, plays nicely with existing Python tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Pragmatic&lt;/strong&gt;: It&amp;rsquo;s opinionated but not dogmatic. You can still use pip if you want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;When to Use What&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;when-to-use-what&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#when-to-use-what&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use pip + venv if&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re writing a simple script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re in an environment where external tools aren&amp;rsquo;t allowed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re just learning Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use poetry + pyenv if&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a large, stable project with complex dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re publishing packages to PyPI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your team is already invested in the poetry ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need advanced features like dependency groups or custom repositories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use uv if&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re starting a new project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want simplicity without sacrificing reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value speed and transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&amp;rsquo;re tired of environment management friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Migration Question&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;the-migration-question&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#the-migration-question&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you have a stable poetry + pyenv setup that&amp;rsquo;s working well, don&amp;rsquo;t migrate just for the sake of it. The pain of migration usually outweighs the benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But if you&amp;rsquo;re starting something new or your current setup feels cumbersome, try uv. The onboarding is smooth, and you&amp;rsquo;ll appreciate the simplicity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code&#34;&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;
&lt;table style=&#34;border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#737679&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#e6edf3;background-color:#0d1117;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# If you want to try uv with an existing project&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;uv init
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;uv add -r requirements.txt  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#8b949e;font-style:italic&#34;&gt;# or migrate from poetry.lock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button
    class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50&#34;
    title=&#34;Copy code&#34;
  &gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Final Thoughts&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;final-thoughts&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#final-thoughts&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Python&amp;rsquo;s dependency management has come a long way. We&amp;rsquo;re past the days of &lt;code&gt;pip freeze&lt;/code&gt; and hope. Tools like poetry and uv have made reproducible environments the default, not the exception.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best tool is the one your team understands and maintains consistently. But if you&amp;rsquo;re choosing fresh, uv is worth a serious look. It&amp;rsquo;s fast, simple, and just works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now go forth and never debug &amp;ldquo;it works on my machine&amp;rdquo; again.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>My non-existing CS Education</title>
      <link>http://localhost:50759/blog/cs-education/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Jun 2025 15:26:31 -0400</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:50759/blog/cs-education/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;Over the course of my career I have self-taught myself a number of topics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting (R, SQL, Python, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine Learning (Linear Regression, Logistic Regression, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Science (Data Wrangling, Data Analysis, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI (Deep Learning, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtualization (Docker, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Linux &amp;amp; Shell commands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But I never received a formal education in Computer Science. And has always bugged me when I would see friends and colleagues with a CS education just grasp concepts which took me a couple of minutes to understand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first resource that I came across which tackled this problem head on was a course designed at MIT to help noobs like me level up, &lt;a href=&#34;https://missing.csail.mit.edu/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;The Missing Semester of my CS Education&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
